{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:dual-coframe","title":"def:dual-coframe","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1445,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:dual-coframe","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:frame-matrix]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:dual-coframe","line":2443,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The Dual Coframe of a Frame]\n\\label{def:dual-coframe}\n\n\\uses{def:frame-matrix, lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular}\n\n\n\n\nLet $(g^{ij}(x))=(g_{ij}(x))^{-1}$. The dual coframe associated to a local frame $(Y_i)$ is\n\\[\n\\varepsilon^i|_x=\\sum_j g^{ij}(x)\\langle Y_j|_x,\\cdot\\rangle_g.\n\\]\nFor a coordinate frame it is $(dx^i)$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The Dual Coframe of a Frame] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6475616c2d636f6672616d65\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aframe-matrix\">↗ def:frame-matrix</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aframe-matrix-nonsingular\">↗ lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(g^{ij}(x))=(g_{ij}(x))^{-1}$\">$(g^{ij}(x))=(g_{ij}(x))^{-1}$</span>. The dual coframe associated to a local frame <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(Y_i)$\">$(Y_i)$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\varepsilon ^i|_x=\\sum _j g^{ij}(x)\\langle Y_j|_x,\\cdot \\rangle _g.  \\]\">\\[  \\varepsilon ^i|_x=\\sum _j g^{ij}(x)\\langle Y_j|_x,\\cdot \\rangle _g.  \\]</span> For a coordinate frame it is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(dx^i)$\">$(dx^i)$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:dual-coframe-duality","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:frame-matrix","title":"def:frame-matrix","label":"def:frame-matrix"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular","title":"lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular","label":"lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:inverse-metric-ambiguity","title":"prop:inverse-metric-ambiguity","label":"prop:inverse-metric-ambiguity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:orthonormal-frames-and-coframes","title":"prop:orthonormal-frames-and-coframes","label":"prop:orthonormal-frames-and-coframes"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:dual-coframe-duality","title":"lem:dual-coframe-duality","label":"lem:dual-coframe-duality"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#exer:inverse-metric-ambiguity","title":"exer:inverse-metric-ambiguity","label":"exer:inverse-metric-ambiguity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#exer:orthonormal-frames-and-coframes","title":"exer:orthonormal-frames-and-coframes","label":"exer:orthonormal-frames-and-coframes"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:dual-coframe","title":"def:dual-coframe","tex":"\\begin{definition}[The Dual Coframe of a Frame]\n\\label{def:dual-coframe}\n\n\\uses{def:frame-matrix, lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular}\n\n\n\n\nLet $(g^{ij}(x))=(g_{ij}(x))^{-1}$. The dual coframe associated to a local frame $(Y_i)$ is\n\\[\n\\varepsilon^i|_x=\\sum_j g^{ij}(x)\\langle Y_j|_x,\\cdot\\rangle_g.\n\\]\nFor a coordinate frame it is $(dx^i)$.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:frame-matrix","title":"def:frame-matrix","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular","title":"lem:frame-matrix-nonsingular","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}